# The band's taste: how the arranger's dice lean in each moment (bandstand::live::taste).
# A row per candidate, a weight per feature of the moment; a candidate's odds are multiplied
# by exp(its score). All zeros: no leaning, the dice as written in chorus.rs and feel.rs.
# Fitted from A/B listening by examples/fit_taste.rs; edit by hand if you like.
#
# Features: bias (always 1); slow (< 150 bpm) / fast (>= 185 bpm); busy / sparse melody
# (notes a beat >= 1.1 / <= 0.72); long form (> 32 bars); the chorus before was the head
# (after-head), stop-time or breaks (after-out), or a solo chorus (after-solo); late (pass 5+).
# For a feel, the after-* columns describe the pass's own chorus.
#
# The soloist's tables ([arc] [idea] [mode] [device] [target]) have their own features: bias;
# slow / fast; the solo's first chorus / its third or later; the chord a dominant / a minor
# (or half-diminished); the solo hot / cool (its chorus shape's heat above 0.66 / below 0.33);
# a dominant resolving to minor. [idea] rows lean picking up the comp, a lick, carrying a cell,
# each against a new idea. Targets: +9 is #9, +11 is #11.

[chorus]
[feel]
